-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2029: workfare; and section 2030, repealed (snap2).
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text; nothing here is verified against it.
-- JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not say.
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars. Hours are numbers. "100 per centum" is 1; "50 per centum" is 1/2.

§ `Section 2029(a): the workfare program`

-- src:2807 | (1) The Secretary shall permit any political subdivision, in any State, that applies and submits a plan to the Secretary in compliance with guidelines promulgated by the Secretary to operate a workfare program pursuant to which every member of a household participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program who is not exempt by virtue of the provisions of subsection (b) of this section shall accept an offer from such subdivision to perform work on its behalf, or may seek an offer to perform work, in return for compensation consisting of the allotment to which the household is entitled under section 2017(a) of this title, with each hour of such work entitling that household to a portion of its allotment equal in value to 100 per centum of the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 [29 U.S.C. 201 et seq.].
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(a)(1) (src:2807-2807)
GIVEN `the political subdivision applies and submits a plan to the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plan is in compliance with the guidelines promulgated by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(a)(1) the Secretary is required to permit the political subdivision to operate a workfare program` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any political subdivision, in any State, that applies and submits a plan to the Secretary in compliance with guidelines promulgated by the Secretary"; the text does not say what the Secretary must do for any other subdivision
    IF `the political subdivision applies and submits a plan to the Secretary` AND `the plan is in compliance with the guidelines promulgated by the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2807 | (1) The Secretary shall permit any political subdivision, in any State, that applies and submits a plan to the Secretary in compliance with guidelines promulgated by the Secretary to operate a workfare program pursuant to which every member of a household participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program who is not exempt by virtue of the provisions of subsection (b) of this section shall accept an offer from such subdivision to perform work on its behalf, or may seek an offer to perform work, in return for compensation consisting of the allotment to which the household is entitled under section 2017(a) of this title, with each hour of such work entitling that household to a portion of its allotment equal in value to 100 per centum of the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 [29 U.S.C. 201 et seq.].
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(a)(1) (src:2807-2807)
GIVEN `the member participates in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of a household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subdivision operates a workfare program under this section for the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2029(b) the household member is exempt from workfare requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(a)(1) the member is required to accept an offer from the subdivision to perform work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every member of a household participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program" in a workfare program the subdivision operates
        IF NOT (`the member participates in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of a household` AND `the subdivision operates a workfare program under this section for the household`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who is not exempt by virtue of the provisions of subsection (b)" and "A household member shall be exempt from workfare requirements imposed under this section"
        IF `s 2029(b) the household member is exempt from workfare requirements` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `s 2029(b) the household member is exempt from workfare requirements` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the member is exempt is not supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2807 | (1) The Secretary shall permit any political subdivision, in any State, that applies and submits a plan to the Secretary in compliance with guidelines promulgated by the Secretary to operate a workfare program pursuant to which every member of a household participating in the supplemental nutrition assistance program who is not exempt by virtue of the provisions of subsection (b) of this section shall accept an offer from such subdivision to perform work on its behalf, or may seek an offer to perform work, in return for compensation consisting of the allotment to which the household is entitled under section 2017(a) of this title, with each hour of such work entitling that household to a portion of its allotment equal in value to 100 per centum of the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 [29 U.S.C. 201 et seq.].
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(a)(1) (src:2807-2807)
GIVEN `the hours of work` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable State minimum wage per hour` IS A NUMBER
      `the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 per hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2029(a)(1) the portion of the allotment the household is entitled to for the hours of work` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): negative hours, or a negative rate, is not work "in return for compensation"
    -- "each hour of such work entitling that household to a portion of its allotment equal in value to 100 per centum of the higher of the applicable State minimum wage or the Federal minimum hourly rate"
    IF `the hours of work` LESS THAN 0 OR `the applicable State minimum wage per hour` LESS THAN 0 OR `the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 per hour` LESS THAN 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`the hours of work` TIMES `s 2015 helper: the higher of two numbers` `the applicable State minimum wage per hour` `the Federal minimum hourly rate under the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 per hour`)

-- src:2809 | (A) The Secretary shall promulgate guidelines pursuant to paragraph (1) which, to the maximum extent practicable, enable a political subdivision to design and operate a workfare program under this section which is compatible and consistent with similar workfare programs operated by the subdivision.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(a)(2)(A) (src:2809-2809)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(a)(2)(A) the Secretary is required to promulgate guidelines under paragraph (1)` MEANS
    -- "The Secretary shall promulgate guidelines pursuant to paragraph (1)": no condition; "to the maximum extent practicable" goes to what the guidelines enable
    JUST TRUE

-- src:2810 | (B) A political subdivision may comply with the requirements of this section by operating any workfare program which the Secretary determines meets the provisions and protections provided under this section.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(a)(2)(B) (src:2810-2810)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that the workfare program meets the provisions and protections provided under this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(a)(2)(B) the political subdivision may comply with the requirements of this section by operating the program` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any workfare program which the Secretary determines meets the provisions and protections provided under this section"; another program, or no determination, is not addressed
    IF `the Secretary determines that the workfare program meets the provisions and protections provided under this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 2029(b): exempt household members`

-- src:2812 | A household member shall be exempt from workfare requirements imposed under this section if such member is—
-- src:2813 | (1) exempt from section 2015(d)(1) of this title as the result of clause (B), (C), (D), (E), or (F) of section 2015(d)(2) of this title;
-- src:2814 | (2) at the option of the operating agency, subject to and currently actively and satisfactorily participating at least 20 hours a week in a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act (42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.);
-- src:2815 | (3) mentally or physically unfit;
-- src:2816 | (4) under sixteen years of age;
-- src:2817 | (5) sixty years of age or older; or
-- src:2818 | (6) a parent or other caretaker of a child in a household in which another member is subject to the requirements of this section or is employed fulltime.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(b) (src:2812-2818)
GIVEN person IS AN Individual
      `s 2015(d)(2)(B) to (F) the person is exempt from section 2015(d)(1) as the result of clause (B), (C), (D), (E), or (F)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the operating agency has opted to exempt a member in a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is subject to a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is currently actively and satisfactorily participating in the work activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours a week the member participates in the work activity` IS A NUMBER
      `the member is a parent or other caretaker of a child in the household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another member of the household is subject to the requirements of this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another member of the household is employed fulltime` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(b) the household member is exempt from workfare requirements` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A household member shall be exempt from workfare requirements imposed under this section if such member is— (1) ...; (2) ...; (3) mentally or physically unfit; (4) under sixteen years of age; (5) sixty years of age or older; or (6) ..." (reading (a): a failed "if"; the six grounds are the whole of the condition)
    `s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds`
        (LIST `s 2015(d)(2)(B) to (F) the person is exempt from section 2015(d)(1) as the result of clause (B), (C), (D), (E), or (F)`
            , JUST (`the operating agency has opted to exempt a member in a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act` AND `the member is subject to a work activity required under title IV of the Social Security Act` AND `the member is currently actively and satisfactorily participating in the work activity` AND `hours a week the member participates in the work activity` AT LEAST 20)
            , JUST (NOT (person's `physically and mentally fit`))
            , JUST (person's `age in years` LESS THAN 16)
            , JUST (person's `age in years` AT LEAST 60)
            , JUST (`the member is a parent or other caretaker of a child in the household` AND (`another member of the household is subject to the requirements of this section` OR `another member of the household is employed fulltime`)))

§ `Section 2029(c) to (f): limits on the work, conditions, job search, disqualification`

-- src:2820 | No operating agency shall require any participating member to work in any workfare position to the extent that such work exceeds in value the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled or that such work, when added to any other hours worked during such week by such member for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity, exceeds thirty hours a week.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(c) (src:2820-2820)
GIVEN `the value of the work the participating member is required to do, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours of work the member is required to do in the workfare position that week` IS A NUMBER
      `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(c) the operating agency may require the work` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No operating agency shall require any participating member to work in any workfare position to the extent that such work exceeds in value the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled"
        IF `the value of the work the participating member is required to do, in dollars` GREATER THAN `the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "or that such work, when added to any other hours worked during such week by such member for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity, exceeds thirty hours a week"
        IF `the hours of work the member is required to do in the workfare position that week` PLUS `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity` GREATER THAN 30 THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only bars; within the limits it does not say the agency may require the work
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2820 | No operating agency shall require any participating member to work in any workfare position to the extent that such work exceeds in value the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled or that such work, when added to any other hours worked during such week by such member for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity, exceeds thirty hours a week.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(c) (src:2820-2820)
GIVEN `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity` IS A NUMBER
      `the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of an hour of work, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2029(c) the most hours of workfare work the agency may require of the member that week` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the value of an hour of work is taken from section 2029(a)(1); a value of nothing or less gives no number of hours
        IF `the value of an hour of work, in dollars` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): negative hours, or a negative allotment, is not addressed
        IF `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity` LESS THAN 0 OR `the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING
        -- the least of the two bars: thirty hours less the other hours, and the allotment divided by the value of an hour; neither below nothing. This is the edge of the bar, not a grant: subsection (c) only bars work beyond it, and the question above (`s 2029(c) the operating agency may require the work`) answers NOTHING within the limits
        OTHERWISE JUST (`s 2015 helper: the higher of two numbers` 0 (`s 2015 helper: the lesser of two numbers` (30 MINUS `the other hours the member worked that week for compensation (in cash or in kind) in any other capacity`) (`the allotment to which the household is otherwise entitled, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `the value of an hour of work, in dollars`)))

-- src:2823 | (1) not provide any work that has the effect of replacing or preventing the employment of an individual not participating in the workfare program;
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(d)(1) (src:2823-2823)
GIVEN `the work has the effect of replacing or preventing the employment of an individual not participating in the workfare program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(d)(1) the operating agency may provide the work` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The operating agency shall— (1) not provide any work that has the effect of replacing or preventing the employment of an individual not participating in the workfare program"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): work without that effect is not addressed by the clause
    IF `the work has the effect of replacing or preventing the employment of an individual not participating in the workfare program` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2824 | (2) provide the same benefits and working conditions that are provided at the job site to employees performing comparable work for comparable hours; and
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(d)(2) (src:2824-2824)
GIVEN `the participant performs work comparable to the work of employees at the job site, for comparable hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(d)(2) the operating agency is required to provide the same benefits and working conditions that are provided at the job site` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "employees performing comparable work for comparable hours"
    IF `the participant performs work comparable to the work of employees at the job site, for comparable hours` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2825 | (3) reimburse participants for actual costs of transportation and other actual costs all of which are reasonably necessary and directly related to participation in the program but not to exceed $25 in the aggregate per month.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(d)(3) (src:2825-2825)
GIVEN `the participant's actual costs of transportation and other actual costs, reasonably necessary and directly related to participation, in the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2029(d)(3) the amount the operating agency is required to reimburse for the month` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): negative costs are not costs
    -- fork F-d3: "but not to exceed $25 in the aggregate per month" is read as a cap on what the agency must reimburse; the text does not say that paying more is barred
    IF `the participant's actual costs of transportation and other actual costs, reasonably necessary and directly related to participation, in the month` LESS THAN 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`s 2015 helper: the lesser of two numbers` `the participant's actual costs of transportation and other actual costs, reasonably necessary and directly related to participation, in the month` 25)

-- src:2827 | The operating agency may allow a job search period, prior to making workfare assignments, of up to thirty days following a determination of eligibility.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(e) (src:2827-2827)
GIVEN `the length of the job search period in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(e) the operating agency may allow a job search period of the length, prior to making workfare assignments` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of up to thirty days following a determination of eligibility"; a longer period is not addressed, and the text does not say it is barred. The wording has no negative ("up to"), which is why the answer outside it is NOTHING while the same module's `s 2029(c)` ("No operating agency shall require") answers JUST FALSE past thirty hours, and `s 2015(h)` ("for a period of up to one year") answers NOTHING past a year
    IF `the length of the job search period in days` AT LEAST 0 AND `the length of the job search period in days` AT MOST 30 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2827 | The operating agency may allow a job search period, prior to making workfare assignments, of up to thirty days following a determination of eligibility.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(e) (src:2827-2827)
GIVEN `the date of the determination of eligibility` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2029(e) the last day of the longest job search period` MEANS
    -- "of up to thirty days following a determination of eligibility"
    `the date of the determination of eligibility` PLUS 30

-- src:2829 | An individual or a household may become ineligible under section 2015(d)(1) of this title to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program for failing to comply with this section.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(f) (src:2829-2829)
GIVEN `the individual or household failed to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(f) the individual or household may become ineligible under section 2015(d)(1) for failing to comply with this section` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for failing to comply with this section"; whether the individual or household is in fact ineligible is for section 2015(d)(1)
    IF `the individual or household failed to comply with this section` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 2029(g): payment of administrative expenses`

-- src:2831 | (1) The Secretary shall pay to each operating agency 50 per centum of all administrative expenses incurred by such agency in operating a workfare program, including reimbursements to participants for work-related expenses as described in subsection (d)(3) of this section.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(g)(1) (src:2831-2831)
GIVEN `the administrative expenses the agency incurred in operating a workfare program, including reimbursements to participants under subsection (d)(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2029(g)(1) the amount the Secretary is required to pay to the operating agency` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): negative expenses are not expenses
    -- "50 per centum of all administrative expenses incurred by such agency in operating a workfare program"
    IF `the administrative expenses the agency incurred in operating a workfare program, including reimbursements to participants under subsection (d)(3)` LESS THAN 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`the administrative expenses the agency incurred in operating a workfare program, including reimbursements to participants under subsection (d)(3)` DIVIDED BY 2)

-- src:2834 | (B) For purposes of subparagraph (A), the term “funds saved from employment related to a workfare program operated under this section” means an amount equal to three times the dollar value of the decrease in allotments issued to households, to the extent that such decrease results from wages received by members of such households for the first month of employment beginning after the date such members commence such employment if such employment commences—
-- src:2835 | (i) while such members are participating for the first time in a workfare program operated under this section; or
-- src:2836 | (ii) in the thirty-day period beginning on the date such first participation is terminated.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(g)(2)(B) (src:2834-2836)
GIVEN `the dollar value of the decrease in allotments issued to households that results from wages received by the members for the first month of employment beginning after the date they commence employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the employment commences while the members are participating for the first time in a workfare program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first participation in a workfare program has been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the first participation was terminated` IS A DATE
      `the date the employment commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2029(g)(2)(B) the funds saved from employment related to a workfare program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a negative decrease in allotments is not a decrease
        IF `the dollar value of the decrease in allotments issued to households that results from wages received by the members for the first month of employment beginning after the date they commence employment` LESS THAN 0 THEN NOTHING
        -- clause (i): "while such members are participating for the first time in a workfare program operated under this section"
        IF `the employment commences while the members are participating for the first time in a workfare program` THEN JUST (3 TIMES `the dollar value of the decrease in allotments issued to households that results from wages received by the members for the first month of employment beginning after the date they commence employment`)
        -- fork F-g2B: clause (ii), "the thirty-day period beginning on the date such first participation is terminated", is read as that date and the twenty-nine days after it
        IF `the first participation in a workfare program has been terminated` AND `the date the employment commences` AT LEAST `the date the first participation was terminated` AND `the date the employment commences` AT MOST (`the date the first participation was terminated` PLUS 29)
            THEN JUST (3 TIMES `the dollar value of the decrease in allotments issued to households that results from wages received by the members for the first month of employment beginning after the date they commence employment`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means an amount equal to three times the dollar value of the decrease in allotments issued to households, to the extent that such decrease results from wages received by members of such households for the first month of employment beginning after the date such members commence such employment if such employment commences" (a closed definition: employment that commences in neither window contributes no decrease, so the funds saved from it are 0)
        OTHERWISE JUST 0

-- src:2833 | (A) From 50 per centum of the funds saved from employment related to a workfare program operated under this section, the Secretary shall pay to each operating agency an amount not to exceed the administrative expenses described in paragraph (1) for which no reimbursement is provided under such paragraph.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(g)(2)(A) (src:2833-2833)
GIVEN `the funds saved from employment related to a workfare program` IS A NUMBER
      `the administrative expenses the agency incurred in operating a workfare program, including reimbursements to participants under subsection (d)(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2029(g)(2)(A) the amount the Secretary is required to pay to the operating agency from the funds saved` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): negative funds saved, or negative expenses, are not addressed
    -- fork F-g2A: "an amount not to exceed the administrative expenses described in paragraph (1) for which no reimbursement is provided under such paragraph" is read as the amount paid, up to 50 per centum of the funds saved; the other reading leaves the amount to the Secretary below that ceiling
    IF `the funds saved from employment related to a workfare program` LESS THAN 0 OR `the administrative expenses the agency incurred in operating a workfare program, including reimbursements to participants under subsection (d)(3)` LESS THAN 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`s 2015 helper: the lesser of two numbers` (`the funds saved from employment related to a workfare program` DIVIDED BY 2) (`the administrative expenses the agency incurred in operating a workfare program, including reimbursements to participants under subsection (d)(3)` MINUS (`the administrative expenses the agency incurred in operating a workfare program, including reimbursements to participants under subsection (d)(3)` DIVIDED BY 2)))

-- src:2837 | (3) The Secretary may suspend or cancel some or all of these payments, or may withdraw approval from a political subdivision to operate a workfare program, upon a finding that the subdivision has failed to comply with the workfare requirements.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2029(g)(3) (src:2837-2837)
GIVEN `the Secretary has found that the subdivision has failed to comply with the workfare requirements` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2029(g)(3) the Secretary may suspend or cancel some or all of the payments, or withdraw approval from the subdivision` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon a finding that the subdivision has failed to comply with the workfare requirements"; without the finding the text does not say the Secretary may not
    IF `the Secretary has found that the subdivision has failed to comply with the workfare requirements` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
